the last Roman King. And that's what happened historically. He named them; he said قَيصر (Caesar) and كِسرى (Khosrow), they would be the last Qaisar and Kisra in that region. And never ever did we have any Qaisar and Kisra in this region.", "Prophet Muhammed said to two of his Companions how are they gonna die: two of them are going to die as Martyrs, and they died as Martyrs, exactly like the prophet said ﷺ.", "The Quran gives a prophecy that is date specific about the Romans and the Persians. The Romans were fighting the Persians 610, 612, 618, etc. They were fighting each other. And then, the Persians defeated the Romans. They took over Antioch, they took over Damascus, they took over Jerusalem, which was the holy city of the Roman Empire, because it was a Christian Empire, and Jesus is from there. So they took over the main point in the Roman Empire. And all Christian historians said: this is the end of the Roman Empire, that's it; the Persian Empire has decimated the Roman Empire; they're never going to come back. And then the (Quran30:1-5) comes and makes a prophecy about the Roman Empire, that The Roman Empire will defeat the Persian Empire exactly in three to nine years, and that's exactly what happened! So how would the Quran possibly know, giving an exact time frame, the two biggest empires of the time? A Bedouin Arab is telling you when they're going to defeat the other Empire?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Lady Skeptical About The Prophet of Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QIxWrKc_J_Y", ((1337, "22:17–22:48"), (1385, "23:05–24:00"), (1444, "24:04–25:00"), (1505, "25:05–25:17"), (1556, "25:56–26:41"),), id: 1208)
