#passage(("The categories of prophecies in Islam are different, many different categories. Some categories would be, for example, about nations that Islam will spread in. Some prophecies will be about specific individuals. Some prophecies will be about developments that will happen. Some prophecies will be specifically about the geology of the earth and how it will change, and stuff like that.", "Prophet Muhammadﷺ said that (you will see the deserts of Arabia returning to being meadows and rivers). Prophet is making two claims: claim number one, that it used to be meadows and rivers; and claim number two, they will come back to be meadows and rivers. Now, we know for a fact that it used to be meadows and rivers. Why? Because if you google right now \"Nature Middle East the greening of Saudi Arabia\", it will show you an article that we find fossils of animals that can only live in abundant water. We're talking about elephants and hippos or whatever. And then they will show you traces of 10,000 ancient lakes that we saw with satellites. They will say, around 5,000 years ago, this deserts of Arabia used to be meadows and rivers. So, Prophet Muhammad didn't have a satellite to look at the 10,000 ancient lakes, or to check the fossils of which animal they are. He didn't have access to any of these things. But he made that claim, and it's accurate.", "Then you can go to NASA; they have an article, it's called \"The greening of Saudi Arabia\". And you can google it right now, and it'll show you pictures of Saudi Arabia, and it'll show you yellow, and it's turning green from 1960 or 70 or whatever till today. It's completely turning green. How is this happening? It's happening, of course, by many factors. Some people will tell you: \"Global Warming\". Other factors, technology: we're able to access the water deep within the earth; technology like they're actually carrying mountains of ice from the North Pole or whatever and bringing it to the deserts of Arabia. Things which were impossible to happen in the past, but they are happening today, which are all fulfilling this prophecy of Prophet Muhammad.", "The Prophet Muhammad named where Islam will spread. He said Iraq specifically. He said الشام (Sham: Levantine), which is Palestine, Lebanon, Syria, Jordan.", "There was an individual who's called Suraqa Ibn Malik, and he was essentially trying to kill the Prophetﷺ; he was a bounty hunter. And when the Prophet left Macca to Medina, they sent him after the Prophet. And then, when he was about to capture the Prophet, something happened and he couldn't: his horse kept sinking in the sand, a miraculous act. He realized there's something about this man, essentially; he's not just a normal human being. But then the Prophet made a prophecy about him, him specifically! He said that (he will hold the bracelets of the Persian King). Now, some people cannot understand how magnificent this prophecy is. Because it's like me talking to some guy in the Eskimos or whatever, and I'm telling him: you will sit in the chair of Trump or something. The Persian King was the strongest man on earth at the time. And this is just a Bedouin bounty hunter in the Desert of Arabia. And the Prophet is telling you: you will hold those bracelets in your hand. And that EXACTLY happened the way the Prophetﷺ foretold.", "Now, that Suraqa Ibn Malik, he became a Muslim. He fought with Muslims. The Prophetﷺ passed away; he didn't die! He could've died of diseases. He could've died in any of the battles. He remained alive. The first Caliphate of Islam, Abu Bakr asSiddiq, took the leadership, and he remained alive. He fought with the Muslims, nothing! In the second Caliphate of Islam, Omar Ibn alKhattab, his time came, and Muslims conquered Persia, and then the bracelets were given to him, and he wore the bracelets, or held the bracelets in his hand, as the Prophetﷺ foretold that he will. And this is a very specific prophecy about a very specific individual. There's so many things that can go wrong. The most important thing is that we don't overcome the Persian Empire, which is the strongest Empire, anyway. But other examples, like I said, is in relation to the guy himself: he could die in many, many other ways.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Attempts To Prove Christianity After Questioning A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ev6mWbHq80U", ((955, "15:55–16:17"), (979, "16:19–17:26"), (1049, "17:29–18:07"), (1092, "18:12–18:21"), (1178, "19:38–20:34"), (1238, "20:38–21:27"),), id: 1209)
