#passage(("The idea of the Roman and Persian Empires, it's recorded in history, which is a non-Muslim, secular history, that is outside the teachings of Islam. So no one can bring that claim: oh, maybe this is just fake.", "There's many that Prophetﷺ made about today: he said, for example, \"the deserts of Arabia will become green again\". Now today, if you open Nature Middle East, they say to you \"[Unveiling] Arabia's green past\", that's what the article is called.", "The Prophetﷺ named the countries that will become Muslim by name; he said which countries Muslims will take over. These openings was after his death -not in his life- so his religion could have easily been disproven after his death. People could have left the religion, and that's it, and they will not take over any of these Empires.", "The Quran explicitly says (Al-Araf7:188) وَلَوۡ كُنتُ أَعۡلَمُ ٱلۡغَیۡبَ لَٱسۡتَكۡثَرۡتُ مِنَ ٱلۡخَیۡرِ وَمَا مَسَّنِیَ ٱلسُّوۤءُۚ (and if I knew the Unseen -the Prophet- that no harm will ever befall me and I will only do good). So he will not be persecuted by his family, his ribs are broken in war, that's not going to happen to him, people are not going to throw stones at him until he bleeds and his feet stuck to his sandals; all of these are actual events happened in his life. So there has to be only selected individuals that come with the Message, but they bring the evidences, for example: the Prophecies of the future.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Intelligent Man Examines The Evidences For Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CyXdIF4BXok", ((2018, "33:38–33:46"), (2026, "33:46–34:04"), (2062, "34:22–35:09"), (2131, "35:31–36:01"),), id: 1210)
