#passage(("Prophet Muhammad himself, or the Quran and hadith, are enough of themselves as evidence for the existence of the creator, because the things that prophet Muhammad did, prophecies that he made, things the Quran mentions, cannot come from a human being; and if they cannot come from a human being, on their own they're also a separate evidence for the existence of a creator. But then, coming back to the points about [splitting] of the sea, or all of these things: these all become secondary issues once there is a creator. If there is a creator, he created this entire world. He's not able to split the sea? He created this entire world; \"he's not able to do this miracle or that miracle\" becomes nothing. This is an outcome of accepting the idea of existence of God. It's where the idea of miracles comes into the picture.", "Now, can any human being know the future? So if we have a man 1,400 years ago, and he's told us tens of prophecies of the future happening, some in his time, some hundreds of years after him and some today, and he's given accurate descriptions, none of them are false, numerous prophecies of the future before the events taking place, and accurate and specific prophecies, and we agreed no human beings can know that, so if we can prove this is the case, then it's the same as me proving splitting the sea, because that's something that human beings cannot do.", "For instance, the Quran has a specific prophecy about the Romans and Persians. The pagan Arabs were people who were polytheist. So they were supporting the Persian empire, because the Persian empire [are] fire worshippers, polytheist. So they were mocking the Muslims, because Muslims are monotheistic religion from Abraham. They're saying: look, our friends, or our allies, are defeating your people. So then the Quran reveals, and it tells us what's going to happen in the future.", "A prophecy by definition is something that hasn't happened yet, in the future. Maybe it doesn't happen. But every claim the prophet makes, the whole religion is at stake. Now, if this is a person who's a liar, who isn't truly a messenger from God, he would make as less claims, and he wouldn't make time bound claims. So he wouldn't be making tens of prophecies about the future, \"this will happen, that will happen\", because he knows the problem of that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Apostate \"Philosopher\" Challenges Muslim On The Existence Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9hau-UgX-0Q", ((1461, "24:21–25:07"), (1507, "25:07–25:50"), (1562, "26:02–26:51"), (1754, "29:14–29:54"),), id: 1216)
