#passage(("Umar ibn al-Khattab, Abu Bakr as-Siddiq and the person himself, Suraqa ibn Malik: there were multiple witnesses. This narration comes from different people. And this happened at the time of Umar ibn al-Khattab, the Second Caliph of Islam. This was well known in the community. That's why other people reported it, because it was well known.", "Now imagine if you were a liar: every claim you make, literally, if it's disproven, the religion is false. And every claim you make, people will say it, because everyone believes you're the messenger of God: \"Oh, the messenger told me this\", or \"I heard the messenger say this about that person\". So, literally, the whole religion is at stake.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Challenges Muslim On Evolution! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hBuaweGxlDg", ((938, "15:38–16:08"), (970, "16:10–16:24"),), id: 1236)

