#passage(("I'm going to read a few verses from Suratul Hajj. The chapter that I'm going to be reading from was revealed in Mecca; however, the verses that I'm going to be focusing on specifically were revealed during the migration to Medina. They were in such a weak state that they had to leave their homes; they had to flee their homes to seek safety in the town of Medina.", "The verse states the following: \"Permission to fight has been given to those who are being fought, because they were wronged, and indeed Allah is competent to give them victory. They are those who have been evicted from their homes without right, only because they say: our Lord is Allah. And were it not that Allah checks the people, some by means of others, there would have been demolished monasteries, churches, synagogues and mosques in which the name of Allah is much mentioned. And Allah will surely support those who support Him. Indeed, Allah is Powerful and Exalted in Might. And there are those who, if We give them authority in the land, establish prayer and give zakah and [enjoin] what is right and forbid what is wrong. And to Allah belongs the outcome of all matters.\"", "The verses include a prophecy, not only of Muslims establishing their prayers and their alms, but much more than that: it focuses on Muslims being given authority on the lands. And this prophecy was made when the Muslims were at their weakest state.",), "Farid Responds, “Proofs of Prophethood 6: Prophecy of Victory to Muslims”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bn-S3xYkev0", ((6, "0:06–0:30"), (33, "0:33–1:18"), (78, "1:18–1:35"),), id: 1244)
