#passage(("\"It is He who sent His Messenger with guidance and the religion of truth to manifest it over all religion, and sufficient is Allah as Witness.\" Now, as we all know, Islam expanded at an incredible rate, from Spain to China, within something like 100 years. That's not really normal: manifesting itself over all other religions, Abrahamic and non-Abrahamic. This is not a prophecy about ending all other religions. It's also not saying that this is always going to be the case. Even if every single Muslim in the world left Islam, it wouldn't make a difference: this is a prophecy that came to pass.", "Now, what makes this prophecy so special is that this is a prophecy that the Prophet, peace be upon him, mentioned when he was at his weakest state. Simultaneously, he was challenging the world. He did not seek the support of a king, he did not seek the support of a foreign nation, and yet he was victorious, and this prophecy came to pass. The proof for Islam isn't in simply the expansion of Islam, but it's with the Prophet, peace be upon him, coming alone from a humble beginning and challenging the world, making that prophecy, making everyone an enemy, calling everyone a disbeliever, and then that actually coming to pass and succeeding, by having Islam manifesting over all other religions. That is proof that he is a prophet.", "There's more to it than that. The Prophet, peace be upon him, made another prophecy after that: he predicted that the nations would gather around the Muslims in the same way that people would gather around a meal. His companion asked: is that because of our small numbers? He replied: no, you would be numerous at that time. And that is the state of Muslims today. The Prophet, peace be upon him, while he was at a state of weakness, prophesies that Islam will manifest itself over all other religions, and then after that will return to a state of weakness, even though they would be high in number. Now that's pretty specific.",), "Farid Responds, “Proofs of Prophethood 14: Prophecy of Islam Spreading”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jaX5kiNcLfA", ((6, "0:06–0:50"), (51, "0:51–2:00"), (122, "2:02–2:47"),), id: 1245)
