#passage(("In all traditions, almost all traditions, the concept of the last hour approaching soon is not limited to a specific time framework. The word soon could actually be applicable to even a period of a thousand or a few thousand years. Because the point of saying that these signs show that the hour is coming soon is not to say that the hour is going to start in 10 days, or in one year, or in 10 years. It's simply to point out the fact that when the hour is established, there is no running from it, and that the life that we lived in this world is going to seem like a day, as it is said in the Quran.", "Also, the idea of Constantinople being reconquered is not far-fetched, for two simple reasons. Because, first of all, it is simply natural and absolutely possible for a state to lose control over a certain territory. Next, the hadiths that pertain to conquering Constantinople are of two types. One group of them pertains to Constantinople's conquering without mentioning the last days. The other group mentions the last days, which is an implication by the prophet Muhammad, sallallahu alaihi wasallam, that there's two different types of conquests. And finally, in a hadith in the collection of [Ibn Majah], we find a hadith that specifies the method by which Muslims will be conquering a city. In other words, they're going to enter the city by simply saying subhan Allah and Allah Akbar. And this is a valid opinion that many scholars held, that the Muslims will be peacefully entering the city, which means that this must be a different type of conquest, since we know that [Mehmed II] conquered it by force.",), "Farid Responds, “[DEBUNKED] Muhammad's Failed End Time Prophecy - Apostate Prophet”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FWYM02LPLcE", ((52, "0:52–1:28"), (88, "1:28–2:35"),), id: 1250)
