#passage(("Prophet was making this prophecy about the countries that would become Muslim. [Sham], that time, included Palestine, Lebanon, Jordan, Syria. [Sham] was under the [Byzantine] Roman Empire. He was not just talking about his backyard or something. It's an area under one of the strongest empires in the world at the time. Prophet Muhammad could not have done these things without being a messenger of God. That's the point I'm making.", "And you cannot use this claim of self-fulfilling. For example, you cannot use the claim self-fulfilling on the prophecy I gave you, the Romans and Persians. He has no control over that. But even this prophecy of countries becoming Muslim cannot be self-fulfilling, because Muslims can try to take a land, and they can do it, it can be extinct; they can lose against the Roman and Persian Empire. It's not just because I say \"we'll take this land, which is under the strongest empire at the time\" that you're going to do it. Self-fulfilling is like I'm saying \"this bottle is going to drop\". That's a self-fulfilling prophecy, because I'm doing it myself. But you cannot do this in this case.", "Now you have an army, you fight; you can win, you can lose. And if you compare the numbers of Muslims, the military weapons that they had, into these two empires, the last thing you think about that you'll be able to do any of that. So you have both the Romans and Persians join together against him. You cannot imagine this. You see the writings of the Romans and Persians: they were like \"these people are not humans that we were fighting against\". Why? Because they knew that he was a messenger of God.", "The prophet Muhammad, his first battle, the battle of [Badr]: the numbers of Muslims, 300; pagan Arabs were a thousand. Muslims had no weapons, because they ran away. The pagan Arabs had horses and weapons and all of that.", "Why would they fight if they don't know? You can fight to survive. You can fight for other reasons. And you can fight