#passage(("Prophet Muhammad, 1400 years ago, made tens of predictions, and they were all right. They all happen. And the challenge is to find something that he said will happen in a specific way and it didn't.", "First, the Prophetﷺ and the Quran as well commands you not to spend money in things which are not useful. So it's not something that the Prophet told the people to do. If you're wasting your money, and people are dying of hunger, the Prophet would tell you not to do that; he will tell you the opposite. So you're not really following what the Prophet says. That's the first thing. The second thing I would say is: how did they get the financial capacity to be able to build the buildings anyway? The Prophet said 1400 years ago that the earth will puke its treasures and money would become abundant within you. So he didn't only say that they would be building these tall buildings.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clever Atheist Pushes Back Against Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dToXMJpuY70", ((470, "7:50–8:01"), (519, "8:39–9:17"),), id: 1253)
