#passage(("To know more now about Prophets and Messengers, we need to have a Scripture and Revelation. That Revelation, we have to assure it's from God, from the Entity that we talk about. So why do Muslims say that the Quran is from God? Many reasons. One example is that prophet Muhammad ﷺ existed 1400 years ago. At that time they had certain knowledge, certain information, they have a certain view of the world. They don't have technology, there's no cars, there's no telescopes. Prophet Muhammad could not read or write, as well. Put yourself in that position: desert of Arabia, couldn't read or write, no technology. And then Prophet Muhammad talks about the future and everything he says happens the way he says it.", "Now, here is the criteria. The criteria is, he makes multiple predictions, tens. They are before the event. The predictions are not self-fulfilling: it doesn't say the book is going to fall and he drops the book. And it is clear predictions: clear and specific, not just vague information like Nostradamus and this nonsense that he used to say. Actually clear things. Now, with these criteria, can any human being know the future 1400 years ago and talk about the future even today?", "Prophet Muhammad, he said, you will see the Bedouin barefoot Arabs. Barefoot: they're not wearing shoes. He's just saying they're very primitive. That's what he's saying by barefoot.", "I'll tell you why it's not general. The difference is, number one, the Arabs were a very primitive civilization. They are not the highest superpower in the world like the Chinese. It's not a fair comparison. The Prophet is talking about very primitive people. Those primitive people were between two biggest empires in the world, Roman and Persian Empires, and these empires were expanding. So you don't even know if, tomorrow, there will be Arabs anymore or they will be extinct. The Arabs were not known to build tall buildings. What the Arabs used to do is to build even in the floor to hide from the heat. The people who were known with buildings is the Romans and the Persians and these type of people. So if you want to make a prediction to be easy, you'll say, the Romans and Persians. And to say, the earth will puke its treasures, and to say that money will become abundant within you as well, when they were poor nations!", "Prophet Muhammad said things like gold and silver. He said gold and silver and things similar to gold and silver. And the oil, today, is called the black gold, literally. The point is, it is an idea of building up. The more predictions are given, the more you know for a fact, he has to be a Messenger of God, because he would not make all of these claims and all of these possibilities will happen to be correct in this way.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Questions Muslim On The Existence Of Evil! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5ov3dkTJn6s", ((710, "11:50–12:25"), (750, "12:30–12:51"), (804, "13:24–13:33"), (851, "14:11–15:13"), (922, "15:22–15:47"),), id: 1255)
