y new comes to the earth, if somebody's born and a new generation is born, they will pass those hundred years, because they weren't upon the earth before that.", "What you're telling me is that it is not impossible during the medieval ages for a person to be born in such tough conditions, when people would usually die when they're 50 or 60 or 70. And this was the [peak age] usually. And seeing somebody live for 100 years was very, very, very rare. There was only one Sahabi that lived that much, according to certain hadits. In any case, what you're trying to tell me is that a person has to be born on that night, because that's the standard of the hadith: people who are on the surface of the earth in that night are not going to live for more than 100 years. So a person would have to be born in that same night and then live up to 100 or more years. Back then, people were not born at such frequent rates as they are right now. And for such an occurrence to happen, that specifically on that night a baby would be born that is going to live up to 100 years or more, is seemingly impossible.",), "Farid Responds, “[DEBUNKED] Muhammad's Failed End Time Prophecy - Apostate Prophet”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FWYM02LPLcE", ((270, "4:30–5:03"), (303, "5:03–5:50"), (425, "7:05–7:47"), (544, "9:04–10:08"),), id: 1294)
