#passage(("If undoubtable evidence was established through Miracles, clear-cut Miracles in front of people, they should not have a choice whether to believe or not to believe, because now the matter is set up. The Quran does mention that: Quran26:4 mentions this idea, that if we were to present them a sign, then فَظَلَّتْ أَعْنَاقُهُمْ لَهَا خَاضِعِينَ (they have no option except to incline to accept that Miracle), because now it's clear-cut evidence.", "We do believe in the Miracles that happened in the past, based again on the same principle: that the Quran is from God. If the Quran was not from God, I would not believe any of this history happened. Since I can establish the Quran is from God, I have no issues accepting that Musa 'Alayhi salam (Moses peace be upon him) performed a Miracle, or 'Issa 'Alayhi salam (Jesus peace be upon him). Not all of the Miracles mentioned in the Bible; I'm saying the ones that are mentioned in the Quran. So it all comes down to whether I can establish whether the Quran is from God or not.", "The Quran has news of the future that no one knew about, that is happening today, that Prophet Muhammad spoke about. It has news of the past that we could not have known, because we did not have access to knowledge of that civilization. We did not have the necessary language to read [hieroglyphics] until we discovered the Rosetta Stone, and that is way after Prophet Muhammad, in the 1800s. The Quran itself, no one able to imitate it in the Arabic language, and this is remaining until today. No Arab has been able to imitate the Quran and its objective challenge, because the criteria is there. Also the life of Prophet Muhammadﷺ himself: looking at his life, and how he could not have been lying, he could not have been deceiving, he could not been insane, he could not have been any of these things, when you look and study his life from a psychological perspective. Evidence of the Natural World: talks about the Universe, talks about things that, if you were bringing it from your own knowledge that time, it would be full of mistakes, because you did not know the things that we know today.", "So when you look at that and you establish all of these types of evidences, you come to the necessary conclusion that this has to be from the Creator. Therefore this itself is a Miracle, because Prophet Muhammedﷺ could not have known this information, could not have done these things that we've said. So if this Miracle is there, then I don't have an issue accepting another Miracle that was done by a different Prophet in the past.", "In the past, other Prophets and Messengers, when they brought these type of Miracles and people disbelieved, Allah punished those Nations: Nation of Aad, the Nation of Lot, Nation of Thamud. All of these Nations of the previous Messengers, Allah mentions their stories in the Quran: that they saw those signs but they still disbelieved, and then Allah punished them for disbelieving. If you see these signs and you disbelieved, then you're doomed, because now it's not an issue of \"I don't know\", because you literally saw in front of your eyes happening. Now it's an issue of arrogance and intentionally disbelieving in the Creator. Therefore you deserve to be punished. So Allah punished many of those Nations that they got those specific type of Miracles happening for them and they still disbelieve.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Irrational Criteria For God's Existence! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xz7nptUD9Ug", ((2218, "36:58–37:21"), (2247, "37:27–37:54"), (2280, "38:00–38:54"), (2341, "39:01–39:16"), (2386, "39:46–40:20"),), id: 1300)
