#passage(("A lot of atheists, sadly, they just say something, and: \"Oh, it doesn't sound nice to me, therefore, I'm going to reject it.\" Rationality doesn't work that way! You have to produce evidence to show us that the moon didn't split, as you claimed it didn't.", "We believe, as Muslims, the moon has split, because we have evidences separate from that, that proves that Islam is from God. Therefore, we know for a fact that this miracle has taken place 1400 years ago. We have eyewitness accounts, reports from people who are Muslims and non-Muslims seeing the incident. In our tradition we have reports. We also have reports of an Indian King who saw this, and he became Muslim. You can critique historically, you can accept, you can say whatever you think about it; either way, you cannot disprove whether this happened historically or didn't happen historically.", "So, for you to claim it's an error, the onus of the claim is upon you, because Allah is not saying this sign was for all mankind, all humanity to see till the day of judgement! This was a sign where some of the Bedouin Arabs challenged Prophet Muhammadﷺ to produce a sign, and this sign was produced to them by God: God has split that moon. So you cannot just say: \"Oh, that didn't happen!\" and then claim it's an error in the Quran.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| The Quran Has Multiple Errors?! Omar And The Pen & Paper Incident| Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_Q0bo07LFNs", ((531, "8:51–9:04"), (547, "9:07–9:40"), (585, "9:45–10:09"),), id: 1328)
// U ML083:391-457 | The Muslim Lantern | 5
#passage(("That's not a prophecy; that's, you can say, a miraculous act the Prophetﷺ did, like we say Jesus walk on water or multiplying food. The Prophetﷺ did many of these things as well, when he was alive, and his people witnessed. Now, one of those things is the splitting of the Moon. But it's not the Prophet, it is God splitting the Moon. We believe all the miraculous acts are happening by God; God is the one doing the acts. Just like when Jesus was doing something, it wasn't him, it was God doing the acts. Jesus had no power on his own (John5:30); he was a human being.", "So, the disbelievers of Quraysh were shown a sign by Prophet Muhammadﷺ. The Moon was parted into two pieces, and then Allah rejoined it after, as a sign for those people to see, to believe. And the Quran mentions that in the chapter alQamar (54:1-2), where it says that (the Day of Judgment has come near, and the Moon has split). And then it talks about the disbelievers: وَإِن یَرَوۡا۟ ءَایَةࣰ یُعۡرِضُوا۟ وَیَقُولُوا۟ سِحۡرࣱ مُّسۡتَمِرࣱّ (If they see a sign, they turn away, and they say magic). So this was the case with the disbelievers of Quraysh.", "What kind of evidence would you like to see of a past event where God has separated the Moon into two parts and then joined it together? Imagine a glass, and the glass splits in two, and then you put some glue, so you can find the crack is still there. That's not a good job of rejoining the cup, is it? Now, God is a perfect being. God can rejoin the Moon and make it whole perfectly the way it was. Why do you need to have a crack on the Moon? I don't get the logic there.", "We don't rely on the splitting of the Moon as a primary evidence why Islam is the Truth; we don't do that. Not only that: the Prophetﷺ multiplying food, or the water gushing out from between the Prophet's hand, or rocks or stones speaking in the hands of the Prophet. I can go on and on. These were things that happened at the life of the Prophets; you cannot see them today, I cannot see them today. So, you can just say, \"I don't believe in that report\", and that's it, and then I don't have anything to prove to you, for a fact, that this event happened. However, prophecies, these are historical realities that I can demonstrate, and you cannot argue back against them. So they're objective in that case.", "That's why if a Christian comes to me and says \"Jesus is God because he's resurrected\", you cannot prove that. You can say that all you want, but you cannot prove that he's resurrected. You cannot say Jesus was God because he multiplied food. You cannot say Jesus was God because he turned water into wine, or whatever miracle you want to talk about. These are all accounts; you cannot prove them to me today or demonstrate them to me to prove that Jesus is actually from God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Attempts To Prove Christianity After Questioning A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ev6mWbHq80U", ((1323, "22:03–22:34"), (1357, "22:37–23:17"), (1412, "23:32–24:17"), (1467, "24:27–25:18"), (1520, "25:20–25:39"),), id: 1329)
