#passage(("Before we talk about my religion, let's first talk about the existence of God. There must be something that brings the universe to existence. There must be a creator, God. Then we move into Islam. There's many, many, many evidences for Islam, and it will all just depend on what you find most appealing and most convincing as an individual. But, for instance, everything relies on the [prophethood]. We agree there is a creator, God that created the universe. Now, throughout history there were so many people that made the claim: we are coming from that creator, we're coming from that entity. You heard about many messengers: Moses, Abraham, Jesus, all of those people. They all came and they had the same claim: there's one creator worthy of worship that created everything, and that we're supposed to obey and worship.", "We believe, as Muslims, the definition of a prophet is someone who receives revelation from God. But they also have evidences to demonstrate that they're actually messengers from God. Because I can come and tell you: Oh, I'm a prophet of God. Thomas comes and says: I'm also a prophet of God. And we have different teachings. So what differentiates truth from falsehood is who has the evidence to bring to prove that they are coming from that creator.", "So Prophet Muhammad, for instance: you can study his life, you look at his message, you look at what he did, how he lived his life. And we know humans and individuals: either lying or saying the truth. Prophet Muhammad claimed that he has the message coming from the creator. Studying his life, you will see that nothing he did would give you any other conclusion other than the fact that he was saying the truth. Why? He did not seek worldly gain. He did not seek worldly power. He refused all of these things in order for him to continue delivering his message from God. One way is to study and investigate the life of the messenger himself. If he wasn't a messenger of God, why would he be doing what he is doing?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Open-Minded Atheist Shifts His Entire Worldview After Encountering A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7wdt9Q4kiMg", ((653, "10:53–12:04"), (729, "12:09–12:27"), (747, "12:27–13:10"),), id: 1339)
