#passage(("The Prophetﷺ claimed to be a Messenger from God, claimed to be a Prophet, and he claimed that he received the Revelation from Allahﷻ. The Prophetﷺ lived among his people for 40 years. And within those 40 years, when he reached the age of 40, he didn't worship idols. He did not accept whatever indecencies they were doing; Allahﷻ kept him pure, to be ready for his Messengerhood. And he used to seclude himself, and go to a cave called the Cave of Hira, and then try to worship Allahﷻ as much as he could. And when that happened, he had Angel Gabriel coming to him, and then the first few verses of the Quran was revealed (al'Alaq96:1) ٱقۡرَأۡ بِٱسۡمِ رَبِّكَ ٱلَّذِی خَلَقَ (Read in the Name of your Lord who Created).", "Now, when that happened, he went back to his people. First, he went back, and then his wife Khadija ؓ, she was calming him down. And then later on, Allah commands him to deliver the Message (alMuddathir74:1-2) یَـٰۤأَیُّهَا ٱلۡمُدَّثِّرُ قُمۡ فَأَنذِرۡ (Stand up and deliver the Message, or warn the people). Now, when he stood up to deliver the Message, he came with a claim. The claim is what we just said: I was in the Cave of Hira, I encountered Angel Gabriel, Jibreelﷺ, and he gave me this Message. Now, that's the claim.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Islam Unveiled: Compelling Evidence For The Truthfulness Of Islam | Chicago - USA | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AUFsBco_CF0", ((387, "6:27–7:24"), (446, "7:26–8:00"),), id: 1341)
