#passage(("Within these words of God, God tells you that the prophets are infallible, specifically in delivery of the message. Meaning that whenever they deliver the message, they can't make mistakes, because they're a representative of God. They're giving you the message of God. So if they speak out of revelation from God, as an authority giving you legal rulings, they're infallible in these legal rulings. If they ever make a mistake, God will correct them instantly.", "And there's many cases where this happens. We see this in the Quran, for example, Hadith. If a prophet were to do something, he doesn't intentionally mean to disobey God, but if he were to do something incorrectly, instantly God will correct him, because it's an example for the people. People are supposed to look at the prophet and learn. Everything needs to be perfect. Everything needs to be done the right way.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Claims That Pantheism Is More Rational Than Monotheism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C3BXt0zJr3o", ((1307, "21:47–22:13"), (1335, "22:15–22:34"),), id: 1346)
