#passage(("You may have a background from Christianity, you may have background from other faith, where they rely on just believe, blind faith, without anything. Islam doesn't function that way. We can have evidences: we can use deductive logic and reasoning, and we can see evidences that this person was a messenger of God.", "Take yourself back in a time machine and put yourself 1,500 years ago in the past. What equipment did we have? No planes, no cars, no microscopes, no telescopes, no phones, no advanced light systems, nothing. People lived in tents, and they had camels and sheep and some water, in the deserts of Arabia, at the time of the prophet Muhammad. Put yourself in that time, that locality, in the existence of the prophet Muhammad, living with his people 40 years; people know him. Revelation from God comes to him.", "Now, in that revelation, in his teaching, you have the following. You have prophecies of the future, of things that happens in his time. He says this will happen, that will happen, that will happen. Hundreds of years after him, and even today, 1,400 years later, these things are happening. So he makes tens of [prophecies] of the future, with what criteria? None of them are false. Some of them are even time bound, giving you time specific what will happen. And he's known to be a true teller. So this is number one.", "Number two: he brings a book, revelation, which has information about the natural world, has information about cosmology, about chemistry, about biology, about [hydrology], about everything. And everything it says, not only is it true, it surpasses everything. We today, with our knowledge, we start learning: okay, the Quran is right about this. We are catching up with the knowledge in a book that came 1,400 years before us, with all advancements and equipment.", "He also tells you things about the past which nobody had access to. They didn't exist in previous Abrahamic text. He couldn't have access, because, for instance, the [hieroglyphics] was not a language that was spoken. We only discovered the Rosetta stone like 200 years ago. So he tells you information about ancient Egyptians that nobody knew, that today we're discovering is true; tells you information about Asia, Mesopotamia, and Abraham and his people, that nobody knew, that today we're discovering: temples buried under the sand, and we realize that what the Quran says is in line with the teachings about what these people used to do.", "So he's doing all of that, and then he brings a perfect system of how to live your life, that surpasses everyone and everything. And he brings the text, the Quran, in the Arabic language, that [redefines] the language, because in the Arabic language you have [prose] and poetry; the Quran has its own category, it's neither [prose] or poetry. And it makes a challenge for anyone to imitate it, produce a text like it, and that challenge has been here for 1,400 years. All the Arabs: nobody has been able to imitate it, and they all submit to that Quran being the highest literature.", "Now we take all of these things into account. Is it possible for a human being to do all of that, and at the same time he says: this is from God, is not from me; only God knows the future, I don't know; God knows how the world is, I don't know; God knows the history, I'm not the person who does? Is it possible for a human being who lived in that time, and only had access to what you can have access to in that time, to bring about these things that I said, if he wasn't truly a messenger?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Surprises Sceptical Chemist With The Evidences For Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z1ousrtPzAE", ((1236, "20:36–20:52"), (1265, "21:05–21:36"), (1296, "21:36–22:09"), (1331, "22:11–22:37"), (1357, "22:37–23:06"), (1386, "23:06–23:37"), (1417, "23:37–24:02"),), id: 1348)
