#passage(("Prophet Muhammad, he lived amongst his people for 40 years. So, it's not like he's stayed two days amongst the people. At that time, there was no social media, so people actually knew other people. You knew the people in your neighborhood. You knew their names, you used to meet them almost on a daily basis, you used to trade with them. It's not like today: today, with social media, everyone is isolated. But back then, people actually knew the people in the neighborhood. They actually knew you as an individual. If you're a liar, everyone knows you're a liar, because people deal with you on a daily basis.", "His people gave him two titles. They called him As-Sadiq Al-Amin, The Trustworthy, The Honest. He didn't call himself that; people called him that, because when they dealt with him, they always knew this guy is the most honest person out there, he's the most trustworthy person out there. When they travelled, they left their belongings with him. They knew that when they came back, they would find their stuff; nothing will happen to their stuff. When they had disputes, they used to go to Prophet Muhammad ﷺ to solve any disputes that happened amongst them. So, this was his kind of biography among the people.", "Then he came to deliver the message of God. What did he call the people to? He called the people to worship God alone. He said to the people: do not worship me, do not worship human beings, do not worship idols, do not worship pictures, worship God alone. Be good to your neighbor; be just, even if it was against yourself, even if it was against your family members. When you're trading, always be just with the people. Do not steal from other people, do not take anything away from other people.", "He was the person who was not looking for anything that is worldly: he was not looking for money, he was not looking for fame, he was not looking for women. The people in his community, they came and they offered him. They said: \"Stop calling people away from idol worship\" (because they were idol worshippers) \"and we'll make you our leader. If you want women, we'll give you women. If you want money, we'll give you money. Whatever you want, you name it, we'll give it to you.\" But Prophet Muhammad refused. He said: Do you see the sun? Bring me a bit of the sun, then I'll stop doing what I'm doing. Basically saying: I'm never gonna stop, because this is for the sake of God, and I'm not looking for worldly things.", "His wife said they used to spend 3 months only living on dates and water. He was in Madinah, he was the leader. He could've said: look, you're my followers, give me some money; and you give me money, and you give me money, and he lives in the biggest palaces out there. But Prophet Muhammad lived the simplest of lives, which shows that this man is a person who is sincere, who is honest. He's not lying.", "One day, the son of Prophet Muhammad died (he was called Ibrahim), and the eclipse happened. The people said: look, this is evidence that he's the Messenger of God, because the eclipse happened when his son died. If Prophet Muhammad was a liar, the first thing he's gonna say is: of course, this happened because of me. But Prophet Muhammad said: no, this does not happen for the life or death of anyone; this is one of the signs of God; when you see it, rush to mentioning God, rush to praying to God. This is not happening for the death of my son or anyone. This is happening as the sign of the Creator, just like everything in the universe is a sign of the Creator.", "Prophet Muhammad spent 13 years in Mecca being persecuted. He was from the most noble tribes, and when he started calling people to Islam, everyone was against him, everyone was trying to kill him, everyone was trying to persecute him. Imagine: you go from being the most noble person, the person beloved by the people, the person called the honest, the trustworthy; when you start calling people to God, now everyone is against you.", "If you're a liar, you're gonna say: okay, I'm gonna stop calling people to God now, because I was in the best place already. I was respected by the people. I'm married to a rich woman, one of the richest women. So, I don't need money, I don't need status, I'm from the best of lineages. So, why would I turn everyone against me just to tell them to worship God alone and stay away from idols, if I'm a liar? No liar would ever do that. No liar would spend 13 years of his life being persecuted by the people to call people to worship God alone, to say to people: stay away from worshipping idols, be just, do not steal, do not do this, do not do that, only worship God, only do everything for the sake of God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “American Asks Muslim Why He Believes In Prophet Mohammed! - Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t0qjjh-k2WU", ((95, "1:35–2:04"), (136, "2:16–2:47"), (174, "2:54–3:14"), (201, "3:21–3:47"), (231, "3:51–4:09"), (253, "4:13–4:47"), (293, "4:53–5:12"), (315, "5:15–5:39"),), id: 1353)
