#passage(("How can you make this objective case for that claim, that Prophet Muhammadﷺ was the Messenger of God? There are many ways to do that. One very simple way is to investigate his claim. He claimed to be a Messenger of God. Prophet Muhammad was born with a group of people who were idol worshippers. They were the custodians of the Ka'aba. He was already married to Khadija; he was running her business; he had money more than he needed. One of the disputes they had, about the Ka'aba and building, is putting the last cornerstone. And they came to him to decide that, which is the most important thing for the Arabs at the time, because they knew him to be \"the Trustworthy, the Honest\".", "Then he had the first encounter with angel Gabriel, where he had some verses revealed to him from the Quran. Then he spent 13 years of persecution: companions killed, him almost being killed multiple times, that he had to leave Mecca and to go to Medina, because they were plotting to kill him. And they didn't stop at Medina; they came with armies one after the other, a battle after the other, still trying to kill him. And he fought!", "And then he lived the poorest, or the most humble life that you could see. When a man came to see Prophet Muhammad, he would be sitting next to his Companions; they will ask: where is Muhammad, peace be upon him? Because he looks like them. He's sitting on the floor; he's not sitting like a king with garb.", "The Prophet told the Companions: \"Do not overpraise me like the Christians overpraised Jesus and made him equal to God.\" A man said to the Prophet: \"What Allah wills, and you will.\" So the Prophet got angry, and he said: \"You don't say that! Did you make me an equal with God? You're saying 'what I will and what God wills' in the same sentence, as if I'm equal with God.\" So the Prophet was very clear that he was a servant. He said: say \"I'm the Servant of God\". So he's a Servant and a Messenger coming from God.", "He died and his armour was rented to a Jewish person. He is the Messenger of God, and he would not use and did not use the fact that he is a Messenger of God to get wealth. There was a narration about them knocking the door of his house, and they only have a date there. And then they gave it to the person asking for food. A date! Imagine: in your house you have no food except one date! This is how he was in his life.", "There was an incident where a woman stole, and she was from a noble tribe, and that's why the people wanted her not to be punished. They said: let's not punish her, she's from a noble tribe. The Prophet said: \"If Fatima, the daughter of Muhammad...\" He didn't say: if Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah. He's not using his status here; he's completely speaking in abstract. He said: \"If Fatima, the daughter of Muhammad, stole, I will be the person to punish her.\" So he's making it clear: you don't do these things; I'm not here to use my status as a Messenger of God, and to do what I like, and not to do what I don't like.", "So, if he was not looking for riches, if he was not looking for status in his community, and if he lived life of persecution (he went to Taif, they threw rocks at him when he was calling them to God, until his feet stuck to his sandals from the blood; he had difficult injuries and almost being killed in many of the battles), now the question is: why he would do any of that, if he was not a Messenger of God? Give me one rational alternative explanation; you wouldn't find any! He called people to worship the same God of Jesus, same God of Moses, same God of Abraham, the same God that the previous Messengers consistently came and taught people to worship.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Surprises Truth Seeker With Evidences Of Prophethood! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JOwaMQoXaBQ", ((201, "3:21–4:28"), (271, "4:31–5:03"), (303, "5:03–5:17"), (321, "5:21–5:46"), (349, "5:49–6:23"), (387, "6:27–7:03"), (428, "7:08–7:44"),)