#passage(("Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, 1400 years ago, he claimed to be a messenger of God. Then it is one of two options: either he's a Messenger of God or he's not a Messenger. There's no third option. And looking at his life, it should be very easy for me and you to determine whether he was the Messenger of God or not: you'll easily be able to find out if he was a liar, and you'll easily be able to find out if he's truthful, because they are the polar opposites of each other.", "So the prophet ﷺ, we can see from his life, he was clearly a sane, trustworthy individual. He had many wives; he lived with them. Imagine having one wife: she already speaks bad of you even if you're good; when she is upset, she speaks bad of you! Now imagine having multiple wives, that none of them have said anything bad about him, in his life or after his death. That is enough of a testimony to his character: that he was a trustworthy individual, he was an honest person. He was the same in his house, when no one can see him, and the same outside, around the people.", "He got corrected in the Quran, and you're not going to correct yourself! His wife was accused of fornication, and the prophet was waiting for revelation! Imagine your own wife! Saying that his wife did something evil is attacking him. But it was more than a month, and there was no revelation coming down to clarify the issue until later on. If you're a liar, next morning you're going to say: look, we have this verse of the Quran that says that she didn't do anything wrong. So, he had all the chances to do these types of things.", "The question is: is it possible rationally for a man who is not a messenger of God to perform and do the same things that Prophet Muhammad did? That's the question that you should have. And the answer to that question should be whether you will be a Muslim or not! Because if the answer is no, he couldn't do it except if he's a Messenger of God, then you should be following what he said, because he's a Messenger of God! So, when he said there is punishment, there is punishment as well if you don't believe. So you will have to put that into consideration.", "And if there is a possibility, then you have to present that logical possibility, see if it's going to be critiqued by Muslims or not. And if it was dismantled, you have no other option except he's a Messenger of God! If it wasn't, then you can say: okay, I've got this critique, no one is able to answer this, it is rational; then I can ignore this possibility, because there's other possibilities.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Questions Muslim About The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LGjHVuCEgbE", ((1438, "23:58–24:30"), (1470, "24:30–25:45"), (1545, "25:45–26:28"), (1598, "26:38–27:05"), (1625, "27:05–27:25"),), id: 1355)
