#passage(("I'll tell you just some of the acts of worship he used to do that is not upon us, because there are certain things which were only for the Prophet, that he would do, which you call khususiya. For instance, the Prophet would fast every Monday and Thursday. I don't have to; it's voluntary. But he would do it every Monday and Thursday. Prophet would pray the night prayer, which can take six to eight hours in the night. He would stand. Aisha [said] his feet would crack from how long he would stay in the night. And she would come and say: \"Oh Prophet, didn't God forgive you? Why are you praying?\" He'd say: \"Shouldn't I be a grateful servant to God? If he forgave me, I should be grateful.\"", "In the morning, there's a duha prayer, which is multiple units as well. He wakes up in the morning, he prays it. 12 extra units he would pray, after and before the five daily prayers. Everything that you can think about from the acts of worship that we would do, he would do 10 times more. Now, if someone isn't a true believer, why would you do this? You go in your house: how long can you act? Can you act for 23 years? Can you pretend for 23 years? Once you accomplish your goal, and you became the leader, and everybody believes you, why are you going to do any of that?", "Plus, I'm not even bringing the fact that he did signs as well, like the messengers do signs: like Jesus healed, Prophet Muhammad multiplied food in the army. The small Arabs in the deserts of Arabia, they were living in this small land. How did they come to conquer land from China to Spain? How? They had nothing: no weapons, no tactics, nothing. But they knew that Prophet Muhammad was a messenger of God. After Prophet died, they fought the Romans and the Persians. They would go with a small stick, and they don't have even the sophistication. They go to the Romans, and the guy using a stick and hitting on the door. That was how they were, but they had God with them. And that's why they succeeded in the end.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Wise Christian Questions The Consistency Of The Teachings Of Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QEeureFKaFM", ((1106, "18:26–18:56"), (1137, "18:57–19:30"), (1170, "19:30–20:11"),), id: 1358)

