#passage(("There was a battle, and the prophet was lining up the soldiers, and there was a soldier who had a bigger belly. So he was coming out a little bit out of the line. So the prophet, he had something in his hand, and he poked him a little bit to just be in the line: don't come out of the line. So that man said, \"Oh prophet of Allah, you hurt me. Give me my revenge.\"", "Now imagine the king of a country comes, and someone in the military, and the king pushes him a little bit with a stick. Nothing. And then that person in the military screams, \"Oh king, you hurt me. Give me my revenge.\" Think what would happen to that soldier in today's world. That's death penalty. The [prophet] then uncovered his belly and said, \"Take your right back. Take your vengeance back.\" And then that man kissed the belly of the [prophet], and he said, \"I only wanted to kiss your belly.\" That's the reason. But look at the prophet. He didn't even think about it. No questions: okay, I hurt you, take your right back.", "You have the people in Mecca, Medina; they would live in towns. And then you had people who would live in the outskirts of Medina. They're very difficult, live in small deserts. They were very tough people, rigid people. This was how they were. One of those Arab came, and he wanted some money from the spoils of war. He wanted money. So he came. The [prophet] was wearing something that had a thick neck, when it comes to clothing. That man dragged the [prophet] from his neck, and then he said, \"Oh Muhammad, give me from the wealth.\"", "Now, how do you think a prophet would react to this? A prophet of God, representative of God on earth, how would he react to this? The companion said that it left a mark on the prophet's neck, peace be upon him, because of how hard this person pulled. Now imagine a king: what would he do? Execute the person, at least, that he would do. You'd have the soldiers execute him before the king even speaks. The prophet laughed. He smiled and laughed, and he said, give him from the money. That was the entire incident. The prophet, peace be upon him, understood these people's nature: the people of the desert, very harsh environment. And this man wanted charity.", "You study the prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him: nobody in human existence can compare. Nobody will read the prophet's life as a sincere individual, looking at what he's done or what he didn't do, and will come to a conclusion, oh, this man wasn't truly a messenger. It's impossible. You need to be a heavily biased person, that you don't want to listen to anything, you're not reading, you're not looking at his life, to come to that conclusion.", "There was a person; he was the head of the hypocrites in Medina when the prophet went to Medina. So there was a group of people who are hypocrites: they're concealing disbelief in their hearts and they're pretending to be believers. This is what the hypocrite is: among the believers as a spy. He's a disbeliever, but he's afraid, because Muslims have power now; he has to pretend that he's actually a believer, and he's a disbeliever. He used to insult the [prophet]: \"Keep your dirty things away from us.\" And that person was coming back to Medina; he said about himself, the honorable person will remove or kick away the humiliated person. He's calling himself the honorable person, and referring to the prophet of Allah as a humiliated person, peace be upon him. This is how he treated the prophet.", "That person died. His son accepted Islam. His son came to the prophet Muhammad and said, \"Oh prophet of Allah, can you give me your garment? I can use it as a shroud for my father.\" And the [prophet] didn't even say anything. He gave him the shroud. Did it end there? Didn't end there. There's a verse in the Quran where Allah says, \"Do not pray on any of the hypocrites.\" And there's another verse where Allah says, \"Even if you seek forgiveness for them 70 times, God will not forgive them,\" because they're hypocrites. [They disbelieved] in Allah and his messenger and died as disbelievers.", "So that son didn't only say, give me your clothing. He also told him, pray on my father. Now imagine: the prophet went to pray on his father. The companions were like, \"Oh prophet of Allah, didn't Allah forbid you from praying on the disbelievers? Prophet of Allah, this was the hypocrite, the head of the hypocrites of Medina.\" The prophet, he said, \"Allah told me, even if I seek forgiveness for them 70 times, he will not forgive them. I will seek forgiveness more than 70 times.\"", "The prophet had a servant who served for 10 years, [Anas]. Look today to people with servants: for just two or three days, if he does something wrong, how do you treat him? \"He never cursed me, he never [scolded] me, he never hit me, and he never said to me once, on something I did, why did you do this, or something I didn't do, why you didn't do this.\" Just think about it: 10 years. He said he was the most generous, he was the most compassionate person to him.", "So that was the messenger, the prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him. Propaganda spread; they say all the stuff, but this was his life. This was how he interacted with his people, the most rude people in their behavior. This is how he interacted with everyone, peace be upon him. So nobody will look at his life, say that he was seeking anything. They came to him and said, \"If you want women, we'll give you all women. If you want money, we'll give you money. You just stop what you're doing.\"", "The prophet, when he died, his shield was pawned to a Jewish person. He had no money. There's no money left. Why would he be pawning the shield to a Jewish person? Why not a Muslim? Why not go to a Muslim and then get money from them? Why Jewish person specifically? Because if the prophet goes to a Muslim, the Muslim will be like, \"Oh, prophet of Allah, I'm not going to take it from you. Take money here. I don't want your [shield].\" He's a messenger of God. People will treat him differently. If he goes to someone, because he is the messenger of God, he will have people who will offer him: take, take. So he wouldn't go to them, because he knows if he goes to a Jewish person who doesn't believe in him, then that Jewish person will treat him like a trade. That was how the prophet was.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Open-Minded Atheist Shifts His Entire Worldview After Encountering A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7wdt9Q4kiMg", ((1234, "20:34–20:58"), (1262, "21:02–21:44"), (1311, "21:51–22:44"), (1367, "22:47–23:43"), (1425, "23:45–24:11"), (1458, "24:18–25:15"), (1517, "25:17–26:24"), (1584, "26:24–27:08"), (1630, "27:10–28:08"), (1691, "28:11–28:42"), (1725, "28:45–29:54"),), id: 1362)
