#passage(("Prophet Muhammad was there 1400 years ago. Now, there are different possibilities on which we can come to, because he made a claim; he said, \"I'm a Messenger of God\". So what are these possibilities? It's either Prophet Muhammad is saying the truth; it's either Prophet Muhammad is not saying the truth; it's either, for example, he could be delusional; he could be getting it from other sources, from Satan or something like that, or another person. These are the only possibilities. If we eliminate other possibilities, then the only option that we have is that he has to be the Messenger of God, because we already know that God exists. And if God exists, then there has to be guidance that comes from It, because everything in the universe is guided. Plants, even the ants are guided. So we are not the odd one out; we also need guidance from the Creator.", "So why Prophet Mohammed could not have been a liar? Prophet Mohammed lived amongst his people for 40 years. They had two titles for him in Arabic; he was called As-Sadiq Al-Ameen. They mean The Trustworthy, The Honest. He was called that by his people. This is prior to him delivering the message and saying I am a messenger of God. People lived with him for 40 years, and in the past people actually knew their neighbors, they knew the people around them, because there was no social media, sitting on your computer the whole day. They actually trade with people; they will know. If someone was a liar, he's already known in the community to be a liar. If someone is not good, does anything bad, it's already known. It's already spread through the community, especially in small communities in the Desert of Arabia. That's the first thing.", "Second thing is, when Prophet Muhammad got revelation, he went on top of a mountain and he said to his people: if I said to you there's an army behind this mountain, do you believe me? They said, we have never known you to lie. Then he said to them, I am a messenger of God. They rejected him. Why? Because he said: stop worshipping the idols, stop worshipping the religion of your forefathers, these rocks that you make with your own hands. They didn't like that, so they rejected him.", "Then Prophet Muhammad had the chance to get anything that he wanted, if he was a liar. If you lie, you would lie for money, women, social status; why else would you lie? He was offered by the richest people in Mecca. First, he had lineage already. He was from a very pure lineage, the lineage of Quraysh. They were the custodians of the Kaaba; he already had that. He already had honor. He was married to one of the richest women in Mecca at the time, and he was doing trades for her. So he had the money, he had everything. But still, when he started preaching his message, they came, they offered him. They said to him: what do you want? Do you want to be a leader? We'll make you a leader over us. You want money? We'll give you money. You want women? We'll give you our women, we'll give you any woman you like. Just stop preaching this message that you're doing. He said to them, do you see the sun? They said yes. He said, bring me a piece of it and I'll stop! Which means I'll never stop doing this, cause I'm doing this for the sake of the creator.", "Some people say Prophet Mohammed could have gotten this from another source. They say the other sources are supernatural power: let's say he saw satan, he saw something. Would satan command you to worship God alone? Would Satan tell you, go to the people and tell them don't worship idols? Would satan say to you, give charity, be good to your neighbors, curse satan? Because that's what the Quran says. Wouldn't make any sense. And wouldn't make sense to say he took it from other people, cause he wasn't literate. He couldn't read or write. So he could not go copy information from the Greeks, from the Latins, from the Hindus, and he was not a traveler, someone who goes to travel all the time and comes back from different cultures. So he could not have copied it from someone else, could not have been lying, and absolutely he could not have been delusional. Why?", "I'll give you an example. Prophet Muhammad's son died, and a solar eclipse happened. The people said the solar eclipse happened because his son died, cause he is a messenger of God! They said, look! It's a miracle: his son died, the solar eclipse happened! If you're delusional, first thing you're gonna say is what? Of course, this happened because of me, I'm a Messenger of God. Prophet Muhammad said, this is a sign of God, it doesn't happen for the death or life of anyone; if you see it, praise the Creator. That shows that someone is not delusional, because if you're delusional, whatever signs are out there, you make up signs to convince yourself of your delusion. Also, prophet Mohammed led armies, battles, fought with different people, married women, and lived with his community. Can you be delusional and fight a war and be a military leader and protect your people? Would that make any sense? So if he could not be any of these things, then what is the only option that he could be? He's a messenger of God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “University Student Challenges Muslim On Religion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0eOxOwACYXE", ((240, "4:00–4:47"), (303, "5:03–6:01"), (361, "6:01–6:21"), (383, "6:23–7:12"), (434, "7:14–7:50"), (474, "7:54–8:48"),), id: 1367)
