#passage(("Prophet Muhammad lived with his people for 40 years before Revelation came. When they travel, you want to leave their goods with someone, they say: okay, we leave it with Prophet Muhammad, because they trust him; then come back, they know they will find their things. This is how the community looked at him. When they had a disagreement: they were building the [Kaaba] in Makah, they had disagreement who places the last Stone, who will put the last Cornerstone. So they went to Prophet Muhammad: can you judge between us, who's going to do it? Cuz he was that respected in the community.", "When Revelation came to him, he came to his people. They were worshiping Idols: you make statues and idols and you bow down to them. So he came and he told them: the Creator, Allah, have sent me; this is not God, don't worship idols, worship the Creator alone. Of course, his people said that we are going to be on the religion of our forefathers, and they tried to kill him for 13 years. Some of his companions were murdered or killed. He had to leave, migrate, go to Medina, because he was going to get killed and die. So in that time, all he was telling the people is telling them about God: to worship God Alone, that there's an afterlife, there's Angels, there's prophets that God sent to you. Would anyone who isn't a prophet of God do any of this?", "And because he said that, he lost everything. His uncle turned all against him. His wife died, actually; his wife was supporting him. Everyone was turning against him; everyone is trying to kick him out of [Mecca] or kill him. Now why would anyone who isn't a true prophet of God turn from being from a royal lineage, with all of the money and everything they want, into nothing? They came to the prophet and they said, stop doing this. The prophet said: it's not in my hand; creator has sent me. If the Creator sent me, the Creator is the only one who can give me permission to stop or not.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim and Christian