#passage(("Prophet Muhammad made the claim, of course: the claim was that he was a messenger of God, the angel Gabriel came to him in the cave and all of that. This is the idea: if you investigated my life, you will come to the conclusion that there are rational options of why I made that claim. You look at my life: I will have a reason. If I say to you I'm a messenger of God, I have something in my mind, whether it is power that I seek, whether it is money that I seek, whatever it is I'm trying to do; it will be a logical purpose, in which I'll be able to trace, looking at your life. And that is the argument that we make: if you look at the life of prophet Muhammad, you'll see all of these other alternative options, none of them can be valid, none of them can work. He cannot be seeking money, because he refused money, and he refused power. [He'd] been living with his wife for two month on the water and dates only, and he could have said, bring me food, bring me money. And he was the leader at the time, but he didn't do that. So if you look at his life, then you start disqualifying these other alternative possibilities.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Pushes Back Against Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cp4X0UcGXDs", ((741, "12:21–14:51"),), id: 1369)
