#passage(("Rasulullah psychology: this is something that Al-Qadi Abu Ya'la points repeatedly to in his Dalail al-Nubuwwah. The prophet, peace be upon him, psychology is not the psychology of a normal person. He says, he always provides these two different possibilities: one, he's either a madman, or two, he's a prophet. He cannot be a normal person. Because who would tell two warriors, \"Return back, because you took an oath to the enemy\"? Who'd say that? Who'd do that? The prophet knew that he has Allah on his side. That is a sign of his faith, his strong faith in Allah, and these are not the actions of someone that was making it up, of someone that didn't truly believe in what he was doing.", "And the proof that he's not a madman, that he is a prophet, is that they actually won. They actually won the battle he promised the Muslims. He was reciting these verses about being defeated in battle before he even had an army. That's number one. And number two is that they were severely outnumbered, three to one. They defeat them. They destroy them. Kill 70 from disbelievers of Quraysh, and capture 70 of their men as prisoners of war. And I think the casualties among the Muslims are like 12 or something like that. Massive defeats for the Qurayshis, for the disbelievers.",), "Farid Responds, “Two Indirect Proofs of Prophethood from One Hadith”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NWVeQBf8snY", ((370, "6:10–7:02"), (424, "7:04–7:44"),), id: 1370)
