#passage(("If you look at the Dalai Lama or Buddha or any of these people, they didn't claim that. They didn't claim to be Messengers of God. They didn't claim they're bringing you God's Revelation and Guidance. And if you claim someone lived such life, you would be saying he's lying. Essentially, that's the only option: he's lying about God, because he's claiming God has sent him something, has communicating to him this text which is the word of God. And if he did, then you have to present reasons for why he would lie.", "So, nobody can make that case, because if anyone makes the case, they'd have to accuse him of lying, because he didn't claim to be a social reformer. And he could have been the best social reformer by accepting their claim: they said you'd be a leader over us if you want, but just stop calling people to stop worshipping idols. So, he'd say \"OK, I'll stop\", and then he could reform the society, and all he wants, he would be the leader. So if he was a social reformer, that is what he would do. So, that makes no sense!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Surprises Truth Seeker With Evidences Of Prophethood! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JOwaMQoXaBQ", ((533, "8:53–9:16"), (601, "10:01–10:26"),), id: 1371)
