#passage(("If the Prophetﷺ was not a true Prophet and Messenger of God, provide me an alternative rational explanation of how was he able to produce this information. This very illogical answer does not work for many reasons. First, it does not respond to all of the claims. Even if he was a trader, he's not going to meet a scientist, a geologist, a biologist, a hydrologist, cosmologist. He's not going to meet a historian, he's not going to meet people who spoke the Greek language. He's not going to meet everyone and collect all that accurate information. If it was hearsay and he was taking from the people that he was trading with, the book would be full of problems. It would be full of the beliefs that the Greeks had, for example, or be full of the beliefs that the Persians had, or the beliefs that the Byzantines had at the time, because he was taking information from them. But the Quran reflects beliefs which are opposite to what these people used to believe.", "It will not also answer the point of the future. Being a trader, you're not going to meet some guy coming with a time machine from the future to tell you what was happening that time. So it's not going to respond to the idea of prophecies. And meeting a trader is not going to help you producing an Arabic text that has its own genre in the Arabic language, the most eloquent speech in the whole Arabic language, that cannot be imitated. That is not going to help you as well.", "So it's an objective fact, an objective reality, that the Prophet Muhammadﷺ is a Messenger of Allah. It's a fact, it's a reality, because you can never produce an alternative explanation that he'd have been able to do the things that he did. By the way, one or two of these things by themselves are enough of evidence to show that he is a Messenger of God. But when you put them all together, it becomes an impossibility that he wasn't truly a Messenger of God, because he didn't claim this is my information; he claimed that this is from The Creator.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-Muslim Claims The Quran Is Full Of Scientific Mistakes?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9P6vTJhCSlI", ((2149, "35:49–37:05"), (2229, "37:09–37:39"), (2294, "38:14–38:41"),), id: 1372)
