#passage(("I was just talking about the miracles of Prophet Muhammad, such as the prophecies of Prophet Muhammad, such as the information of the past, such as the Quran, which is a living miracle till the end of time, such as all of the information about the life that we are studying and looking at. All of these are the evidence I'm giving you. All of these are miracles by definition. Quran is the biggest miracle, of course! Can any human being tell you the future specifically and clearly, and make tens of prophecies, all of them are accurate, if he wasn't sent by God, if this information doesn't come from God? Can human beings do it on their own? Is that possible? This is one example of a miracle.", "But evidence does not only need to be a miracle. We can also use our God-given common sense and rationality to come to a conclusion that something is true. Using rationality and common sense, you cannot deny the fact that Prophet Muhammad was a Prophet of God after studying his life. So, if you want to say he isn't a Messenger of God, and you believe in God, and he came and he told people to worship God alone (anNisa4:36), and he told people to give charity (alMunafiqun63:10), and he told people to believe in Jesus and Moses and Noah (alAhzab33:7), and Satan is your enemy (Fatir35:6), and all of these things, you're going to have to tell me, why was he doing that? You're going to have to give me a rational reason, an explanation to why would he be doing that, if he wasn't a Messenger of God. And why would God allow him, of course, to continue in doing that, as well? Because God exposes false Prophets. He exposes liars.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Attempts To Prove Christianity After Questioning A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ev6mWbHq80U", ((1587, "26:27–27:58"), (1688, "28:08–29:29"),), id: 1374)
