#passage(("He got a revelation just like Moses got a revelation from God, Jesus has a revelation from God. Angel Gabriel, the same angel that came to Mary, that came to the other prophets with revelation, came to Prophet Muhammad, revealed to him the revelation from Allah, the Quran, and then he came to his people.", "Let's do this thought experiment. Hypothetically, let's say Prophet Muhammad came up with this idea, it wasn't from God. Why he would say to the people, \"I'm a messenger of God,\" if he wasn't truly a messenger of God? It could be for power.", "Prophet Muhammad, when he started calling to his message, he was respected in the community, cuz he lived 40 years before revelation. Now, when the message came, and he came to his people, he went up on top of a high place or a mountain and said to the people, \"If I said to you there's an army behind the mountain, would you believe me?\" They said, \"We've never known you to lie.\" Then he said, \"I'm the messenger of God.\" Then they rejected him.", "Then for 13 years, they were persecuting him, trying to kill him. They killed some of his companions. Sumayya was killed. Bilal, all of the companions were being tortured or killed. He himself, multiple times they tried to kill him. There's this instance where the prophet was praying, and he was [prostrating] and someone came and put his leg on the neck of the prophet trying to suffocate him. So, when he was honorable, respected, and loved, he turned into being persecuted by the own people, his family members; his own uncle is the one who's trying to do this to him.", "Then, the prophet had to go to Medina. Why? They're going to kill him. The tribes came together, plotted to kill the prophet. So, Allah revealed to the prophet to leave, because they're plotting to kill you. Then they continued attacking him.", "Now, when he was in Mecca, the leaders of Quraysh, they came and they said, \"If you stop this, we'll give you anything you want. If you want to be the leader, we'll make you a leader over us. If you want women, we'll give you our woman; choose from wherever you want, we'll give her to you. If you want money, we'll give you all the money you want. Just stop calling to this message.\" They came to him and they said, \"We'll listen to you. You worship our God for one day, we worship your God for one day. Let's compromise.\" Prophet said, \"No. This is not in my hand. This is a revelation that comes from God.\"", "Prophet was with Aisha, his wife. The narration says for two months they lived on dates and water. Nothing. A poor person would come and knock the door, and Aisha, she'll find one or two dates in the house and she'll give her one. The messenger of Allah, if he said to anybody, \"Give me food,\" they'll give him food. But he wouldn't do it, because he's not using this religion for the sake of power.", "Prophet Muhammad came, and the companions wanted to prostrate to him. They said, \"We saw the Christians and the Jews, they prostrate their patriarchs and their kings.\" So he forbade them; he said, \"No, you only prostrate to God; don't prostrate to me.\" Where is this power that he's seeking? What would be the power? So he couldn't be seeking power.", "So Prophet Muhammad's life was like that. He lived a life where he sacrificed everything for the sake of this religion. He went to Ta'if; they threw stones at him until he bled and his feet stuck to his sandals. He could have died.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Wise Christian Questions The Consistency Of The Teachings Of Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QEeureFKaFM", ((571, "9:31–9:47"), (590, "9:50–10:08"), (612, "10:12–11:15"), (677, "11:17–11:46"), (709, "11:49–12:03"), (723, "12:03–12:37"), (760, "12:40–13:02"), (809, "13:29–13:48"), (863, "14:23–14:34"),), id: 1378)
