#passage(("If the Prophetﷺ is not a true Prophet of God, what would he be? False Prophet, meaning what? He's lying, let's say, or he's learning from Satan. You cannot say he was crazy or delusional. He was clearly leading armies, he led whole communities. So these are very ridiculous claims that shouldn't be even entertained. But the only claims that can be entertained is to claim that he was not saying the truth, meaning he was lying, or he was learning it from Satan, which also means he's lying in a way, or he was deceived by Satan, which means he's not lying, but he's given you the teaching of Satan.", "So first, lying: what would he lie for? Let's test this hypothetical situation: Prophetﷺ was lying because he was seeking power. Prophetﷺ was respected in his community; they had two titles for him (before Revelation): they used to call him الصادق الأمين, the trustworthy, the honest. When they were building the Kaaba (in which they believed was a holy place of God), when they had a dispute on who places the last stone, they went to Prophet Muhammadﷺ. He already had a say in the community. They went to him because he was the trustworthy, the honest, and they respected him and respected his decision. Then he said to each group, \"You hold a part of the cloth, and we put the stone, and both of you hold it,\" and then he put the stone himself. So this was how his community looked at him.", "When the son of the Prophetﷺ, Ibrahim, died, and then there was an eclipse happening, the people in the community, they said that this is evidence that he's a Prophet of God, because when his son died the eclipse happened! What would a liar say in this situation? \"Yeah, of course! You see! God made the eclipse for me! You should follow me and believe in me now!\" That's what a liar would say.", "The Prophetﷺ said the exact opposite. He said (this is a sign from God that does not happen for the life or death of anyone). He said (if you see it, you rush to thanking God and praying and prostrating to God). This does not happen because of the death of my son or the death of anyone, or the life of anyone; this is a sign that God does. They already are the one who's saying this has happened because of his son. He doesn't even have to make the claim; all he has to say is, \"Yes, you're right!\"",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Orthodox Christian Questions Muslim About Islamic Conquest! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ob9CNiMiKAE", ((303, "5:03–5:49"), (356, "5:56–7:00"), (475, "7:55–8:13"), (493, "8:13–8:34"),), id: 1379)
