#passage(("In the case of Prophet Muhammadﷺ, he came with that Message. We already believe in a Creator in this case; we're not discussing the belief in a Creator. Now, he could have not said the Truth. Why do people lie, usually? Being scared of something, for instance; financial gain; power in the community; to make a change. These are the reasons why people will say something which isn't true.", "They came to the Prophet Muhammadﷺ. They told him, you stop this mission that you're doing. But the Prophet Muhammadﷺ, he said, do you see the sun? (In the authentic narration, because there's many people who quote a different narration; this is the most authentic wording.) Bring me a piece of that sun. If you're able to bring me a piece of that sun, then we talk! Meaning, I'm commanded to do this by God. This is not something that I'm doing for my own purposes.", "And you see that reflected even more when the Prophetﷺ was in the Medina period. Prophet Muhammadﷺ died and his shield was مرهون, he did رَهن (mortgage) of his shield, with a Jewish person. The shield, he was given it to a Jewish person to use it, rent it, and then give him money. Now the question is: Prophet Muhammadﷺ at that time, he was the leader of the Muslims and he had the money, could have said to Abu Bakr, 'Umar.. Abu Bakr asSiddiq was rich! 'Uthman, may Allah honour him, was rich! Give me money!", "Prophet Muhammadﷺ, the scholars explained, the reason he did that is because of his shyness from asking people for money. He's not using the fact that he's a Messenger of God as a means to get money from people. He didn't do that, which is why he rented; he went to someone who's not a Muslim, because if he goes to a Muslim, \"Oh Prophet of Allah, take all what you want! Everything, you just ask for it, I'll give it to you.\" And he will refuse to take anything from the Prophetﷺ because he is the Messenger of Allah. So he went to someone who's not a Muslim, who doesn't believe in his Messengerhood, because he will deal with him justly in that way, and he's not going to try to give him everything.", "When you look at the life of the Prophetﷺ, it's not just before the Message, but also after that. So after the Prophet Muhammadﷺ was already established and having all of this power, he also was not seeking financial gain, was not seeking money, was not seeking women, even though he could have gotten whatever he wanted. So we know from that that this could not have been the case.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Islam Unveiled: Compelling Evidence For The Truthfulness Of Islam | Chicago - USA | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AUFsBco_CF0", ((555, "9:15–10:07"), (622, "10:22–11:10"), (674, "11:14–11:46"), (709, "11:49–12:20"), (747, "12:27–12:50"),), id: 1381)
