#passage(("Also, some people will say that he was trying to rectify the community. They came and offered him authority and power, and if he wanted to rectify the community, it was the first thing you need to do: take the authority and power, rectify the community, story's over! But the Prophetﷺ refused that. And not only that: if you want to rectify the community, you want people to come closer to you. You're not going to start telling them \"your Book is corrupted\" (the people of the Book), \"Jesus didn't die\", \"there's no trinity\", \"the Jewish people worship the Rabbis\". Are you going to tell them that? Or are you going to tell them that which brings them closer to you, so you can rectify a community? Which shows the Prophetﷺ was saying the Truth, whether people liked the Truth or did not like the Truth.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Islam Unveiled: Compelling Evidence For The Truthfulness Of Islam | Chicago - USA | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AUFsBco_CF0", ((891, "14:51–15:29"),), id: 1382)
