#passage(("It's always a recycled source. They go to one or two YouTubers and they listen to what they say. Then, they come thinking they have an argument, and tell it to all the Muslims, and they get refuted. Even though those same YouTubers that they talk about have been refuted numerous times on YouTube, they still go thinking that these things are not refuted.", "These things are different from one another. Being delusional is not the same as being bipolar. It's not the same as having delusions of grandeur. These are all separate things that mean separate things, that should show separate symptoms. You will get idiots like this: they've never studied psychology or anything to do with psychological disorders, and they will come and become the doctors of the 21st century! They become the father of modern psychology all of a sudden, and they want to tell you, \"This is my professional analysis of how Prophetﷺ was.\"", "I simply sit back, I'm relaxed, and then I say, \"OK, you define to me what is the meaning of schizophrenia? What are the signs of schizophrenia? So that we can then look at the Prophetﷺ. And then give me evidences, where these signs are actually there.\" Because I should not take any claim seriously until you first provide me with the reasons: what is your claim, and where is the proof of your claim? So that I can respond to you to begin with. How can I respond to an empty claim? They don't know the definition or the symptoms, but they're just making the claim because they don't want to accept the Prophet Muhammadﷺ as a Messenger of God. Then, why would I waste my time on them either?", "If they were delusions, did he just have a vision and that's it? Or did he have a vision that contained information? There was the Quran, there was literature which we're presenting already today to be from God. If he had encounters to get revelation, that was the encounter, and he recited the revelation after he got the encounter. So, if he was delusional, then what you should be doing is investigating the text that came and proving that he was delusional, he was just making up certain things. Then, the Arabs would have brought something like the Quran, and people would have already disproved it for 1,400 years, if it was just delusional, and not an actual revelation coming from God.", "And all the Messengers of God received revelation! Even that Christian who believes in Christianity has to believe that all the Prophets of God have received revelation, inspiration from God.", "Now, the idea of illusions of grandeur, as another example: you would look at his life. He is spending two months without food, just water and dates, his wife says. The fact is that, when people entered, they used to not know who the Prophetﷺ was; they used to ask, \"Where is Prophet Muhammad?\" Because he's sitting, he looks like everyone else. There's no chair where he's sitting on as if he is the king, he's the master, he's the leader. The Prophet forbade his Companions from standing up to him when he enters, because there was this habit that the kings used to do: the Roman and Persian kings, whenever the king enters, everyone stands up. So, they said, \"We want to do the same\"; the Prophet forbade them: \"You don't stand up for me.\" Does this sound like someone who's got the delusions of grandeur?", "And this genius Christian is the one who discovered that he's got this psychological disorder, and two billion Muslims, who have been following him, and the people who died for him, who lived with him, they did not notice it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Questions The Historical Existence Of Prophet Mohammed! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fYl53WeiaSk", ((369, "6:09–6:19"), (396, "6:36–7:25"), (445, "7:25–8:06"), (506, "8:26–9:02"), (544, "9:04–9:09"), (618, "10:18–10:56"), (696, "11:36–11:42"),), id: 1388)
