#passage(("In the Bible, the people were saying about Jesus that he's from Satan. Then what did Jesus say to respond to them? He said (Matthew3:25-26) (the house cannot be divided against its own self). Meaning: what he's saying to them is that Satan is not going to teach you things that go against Satan. If Satan is the one who is telling me this, he's not going to tell you the things I'm telling you, because these things are good, and Satan teaches you to do bad, so it's impossible for me to be someone from Satan.", "The Prophetﷺ came, and his people, all of them, were Idol worshippers. Does Satan like Idol worship or does he hate Idol worship? So why would he teach Prophet Muhammad: go to these people and say to them, stop worshipping Idols, fast for the sake of God, free servants and slaves, do not have racism amongst your community and Society? Would Satan be doing this? So it's impossible for it to be Satan, unless this is a good Satan, a Satan that wants good for the people. So it is impossible for you to say that this is from Satan.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Orthodox Christian Questions Muslim About Islamic Conquest! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ob9CNiMiKAE", ((546, "9:06–9:33"), (578, "9:38–10:34"),), id: 1389)
