#passage(("Your own personal experience does not negate the fact that the evidence of Islam makes it true.", "But let's assume that was true, and that was the case: does that negate the fact that Prophet Muhammad presented evidence that he's a Prophet of God? If he presented evidence that he was a Prophet of God, why does it matter if an angel did something new in this encounter? How does that change the fact that he's a Prophet of God?", "The evidence that he had the encounter: prophecies of the future, the knowledge about the history, the knowledge about what God created, the Earth, the Moon, the stars, all of these things. So, all of these things that are mentioned in the Quran and in the Hadith are the evidence. So, that proves the encounter by default, because if he didn't have the encounter, he wouldn't be able to bring these things. It's as simple as that! If this encounter wasn't true, that he didn't have divine Revelation, he wouldn't be able to bring divine knowledge. So, if there is divine knowledge, you've already established the encounter is true.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Attempts To Prove Christianity After Questioning A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ev6mWbHq80U", ((2187, "36:27"), (2233, "37:13–37:31"), (2263, "37:43–38:14"),), id: 1392)
