#passage(("The Bible says the devil will appear to you as an angel of light (2Cor11:14); Paul is saying this. Do you know what Paul saw in his vision to Damascus? He saw light! (Acts9:3-4) So, if anyone is concerned about the devil coming to you, you should be concerned about Paul following the devil. When it comes to Prophet Muhammadﷺ, he didn't see light, and we don't say Angel Gabriel is the angel of light. So this verse doesn't apply in any way, shape or form. I don't understand how Christians read this stuff, and they don't see that. They should have a problem with Paul before they talk about Prophet Muhammad, because he's the one who saw light in his vision to Damascus and heard a voice. So, he saw the devil coming to him, and people are still following Paul.", "Prophet Muhammad saw Angel Gabriel. Angel Gabriel came to Prophet Muhammad; Prophet Muhammad was frightened, because you're seeing an extraterrestrial being. Me and you, we don't see angels; they're not of the creation of this life that we see. Something that is extraterrestrial, so you're going to be frightened, of course. Then the angel pressed the Prophet to calm him down, and then he gave him verses of the Revelation. But that was only the first encounter. Then the angel Gabriel came to Prophet Muhammadﷺ throughout his 23 years of revelation, and he gave revelation to the Prophet. So where is the issue?", "Angel Gabriel came in a form of a human being. He had very dark hair. There's multiple encounters where the Companions saw the Prophet receive Revelation from God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Wife Grills A Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tUX4xfgST_E", ((1799, "29:59–30:48"), (1853, "30:53–31:30"), (1926, "32:06–32:28"),), id: 1393)

