#passage(("Now, the funniest thing is, everything he said is applicable to the Bible. This is not about Christianity, but we're using the same argument. \"The foundation is not built on sand\"? But the foundation of Christianity is built on sand! Give me one eyewitness account to the Crucifixion of Jesus! And don't bring me the Bible, which is written by people 3-4 hundred years later (the earliest carbon dating you have), and tell me that's an eyewitness account!", "And the funny thing he says: \"Give me an eyewitness account to the first encounter of Prophet Muhammad with Angel Gabriel.\" But he knows in the first encounter the Prophet was alone, so how can I give you an eyewitness to that? What kind of a ridiculous statement is that? But that's not really what he's asking. He's trying to say: give me an eyewitness account of the Prophet with an Angel where he received Revelation, because we cannot base everything just on that encounter. But there are MULTIPLE encounters where Prophet Muhammadﷺ gets Revelation from God, or the Angel Gabriel comes and his Companions see him.", "'Aishaؓ, his wife, saw the Prophet Muhammadﷺ receiving Revelation, and it would be in a cold day, a cold day in the Desert of Arabia, and he would be sweating. His thigh was on the thigh of one of the Companions, and he felt the weight of the Revelation coming down, and he felt like his thigh was going to break from the heaviness of Revelation.", "Angel Gabriel came in the form of a man to the Prophet Muhammadﷺ, and we have a mass reporting of this event from 'Umar ibn alKhattab, from other Companions. They were sitting down, and Angel Gabriel came, and he asked the Prophet Muhammad some questions to teach the Companions about the religion. And they observed him, and they described him as a man they have never seen before, coming with very dark hair, very white cloth; there's no signs of travelling!", "Why are they saying this? Because if it's a new person that we don't know of the community, how did he travel here, and he has no signs of travelling? Nobody saw him come in or out! Because he was Angel Gabriel coming to Prophet Muhammad. And then the Companions saw him directly talking to Prophet Muhammad, and teaching people the religion. And there were other encounters. We have many encounters of that happening.", "Now YOU will have ZERO eyewitness account to the Crucifixion and the Resurrection, the Resurrection more importantly than the Crucifixion! So apply this 'foundation of sand' to your own Faith.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| PBD Calls Me An Islamist?! Five Reasons To Debunk Islam?! | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S1CSlMRuy9s", ((1652, "27:32–28:01"), (1687, "28:07–28:34"), (1718, "28:38–28:57"), (1740, "29:00–29:20"), (1764, "29:24–29:43"), (1787, "29:47–29:56"),), id: 1394)
