#passage(("There's no such thing as mention by name, but the description can be given. If the description is given and the description is fitting the individual or the person, then it would make sense for us to accept that this person is prophesized in the Bible.", "For example, hypothetically, it mentions that there's going to be a prophet that is going to come, and he's going to specifically come to the Arabs, and it mentions something in the geographic location, say a mountain or a place or a land, and it mentions what he will do: that he's going to go to idol worshippers, because the people at the time of the prophet were idol worshippers, and he's going to defeat them, and that he's going to bring a new revelation, new law, something completely new, not of the past law, and he's going to come to all people. The prophets were sent to the children of Israel; no, he's going to come to the Gentiles, everyone. This is literally the life of the prophet. There's nothing really missing at this point. So if there is such a detailed description, then you would agree that prophet Muhammad is a messenger of God.", "So it's the idea of accepting the principle before going to the verse, because if you reject the principle, then I will ask you: why do you reject the principle? Your argument was all based that he's not mentioned: if he's mentioned, I would accept him. If there is this clear description hypothetically, then would you accept him? If you say no, then we see the clear inconsistency here: there's no sincerity, the person is just arguing for the sake of argument. So that is why I'm asking you before I'm taking you to the verses.", "But there is that description I gave you, exactly in the Old Testament, specifically Isaiah 42. The whole chapter is about what I just told you. It's about a messenger that is going to come.", "Now when someone wants to be misleading, they tell you something and they don't give you the reference. You know why they don't give you the reference? Because they don't want you to go and look. And it's not a verse, it's a chapter. When you come and say the verse doesn't say that, I didn't say a verse says that. I said the chapter holistically says what I just told you. It talks about all the points that I've described. It's all mentioned in the chapter.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Overconfident Christian Meets The Wrong Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EFSTD9c3Lec", ((66, "1:06–1:20"), (100, "1:40–3:11"), (206, "3:26–4:00"), (240, "4:00–4:12"), (354, "5:54–6:30"),), id: 1426)
