#passage(("I already gave you an example refuting you in Deuteronomy. Deuteronomy 33:2 talks about Moses coming from Mount Sinai, and it mentions Yahweh, the word Yahweh, word for word. Go to the Hebrew, it will tell you explicitly Yahweh: \"Yahweh from Sinai came down.\" The word Yahweh is used for the representative of the Lord, in this case, which is Moses, a prophet of God. Just because the word in Isaiah 42 says Yahweh doesn't mean that it's God himself. It can easily mean a representative of God. How do we know it's a representative of God? We already see the whole chapter talking about that representative of God that God is sending. The whole chapter is talking about the person is going to come, and what he's going to do and what he's not going to do.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Overconfident Christian Meets The Wrong Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EFSTD9c3Lec", ((3579, "59:39–1:01:20"),), id: 1428)
