#passage(("I don't like using the Bible to prove Islam, because we have our own evidences to prove why Prophet Muhammad is a prophet. We don't need to use the Bible. However, if you're asking me, if we look at the Bible, can we find the prophet? It is mentioned in the whole chapter of Isaiah 42.", "This is a description of a prophet to come in the future. This is a belief of Christians and Muslims: they believe that this is a prophecy of someone to come in the future. This prophet is sent to non-Jews. So it cannot be Jesus, for example. It cannot be Moses, because they were sent to the Jews. The Tawra of Moses is already there in Isaiah, but this person is going to bring a new Tawra.", "Now, if you continue reading on, then you will see: \"Let the people of Kedar rejoice.\" Khedar is the son of Ishmael, one of the sons of Ishmael, which refers to the Arabs. Who says that? It's in Genesis 25:13. Genesis 25:13 will tell you the children of Ishmael, and then it will mention Nabayoth and it will mention Kadar, who are the Arabs. Then he mentions mountain tops and Salah. Do you know where mountain Salah is? It's in Saudi Arabia, Medina, few kilometers away from prophet's mosque specifically.", "If you continue reading, it will tell you: do not be blind to the messenger who I sent. So my advice to you is the same advice in these verses: do not be blind to the messenger of God.", "There's actually some Jews that believe that this is about Prophet Muhammad, but they say, \"Oh, he's only for the Arabs.\" But he said he wasn't only for the Arabs. So how can you say he's a true prophet and then say he's lying? They don't really need this verse, because they wait for their messiah to come anyways.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Passionate Christian Challenges Muslim On Jesus & Salvation! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X5mvbKQDRZI", ((2341, "39:01–39:27"), (2399, "39:59–40:52"), (2452, "40:52–42:32"), (2618, "43:38–43:53"), (2691, "44:51–45:11"),), id: 1429)
