#passage(("If I were to bring an example of a Prophecy about Prophet Muhammad, there is nothing more clearer that can be done, because it doesn't only pinpoint his description: the description not only fits him, but even pinpoints where he's going to come, and what his Message is. This is what I would say is a clear Prophecy: pinpointing his lineage, where his lineage he's going to come from, which people he's going to go to, what is he going to bring, and what he will say to these people, and what will happen between him and them. All of these things are in the Prophecy that I'm talking about.", "I have the Interlinear. So it says (Isaiah 42:1-4): \"Behold, my servant, whom I uphold; my chosen, in whom my soul delighteth: I have put my Spirit upon him; justice he will bring forth to the Gentiles.\" \"Not he will cry out\": he's not going to say, \"My Lord, my Lord, why have you forsaken me\" (Psalms 22:1); he's not going to do that. \"Not he will cry out, nor raise his voice, nor cause to be heard in the street his voice.\" This is verse 2. Verse 3: \"A reed bruised not he will break, and flax smoking not he will quench. For truth, he will bring forth justice.\" Verse 4: \"Not he will not fail, nor be discouraged, until he has established in the earth, justice. For his Torah\" (in the Hebrew, which is Law). The word is \"Torah\" literally. So he's going to bring a \"Torah\" with him. \"The coast lands shall wait\": so the world, everyone is going to wait for his Torah, for his new Law, that he's going to bring.", "Then here it says: \"To open the blind eyes, to bring out the prisoners\" (Isaiah42:7). So he will bring people out from darkness. And then 8 says: \"I am Yahweh, this is my name: and my glory to another, I will not give, nor my praise to carved images.\" This person is coming to people who worship idols, they worship images, they worship statues.", "Now (Isaiah42:9-10): \"The former things, behold, have come to pass, and new things I declare: before they