إِلَى النُّورِ (Ibrahim14:1) (So he can take them out of darkness into light). Literally this is what the Quran term uses for Prophet Muhammadﷺ.", "(Isaiah42:17) \"They shall be turned back, they shall greatly be ashamed.\" So they will lose against this man of war, like Prophet Muhammadﷺ fought against the pagan Arabs. Why did he fight against the pagan Arabs? Because they were worshipping idols. And then it says explicitly: \"they shall be greatly ashamed, those who trust in graved images, who say to the molded images, you are our gods.\" And then it mentions (Isaiah42:18-19): \"You deaf, hear you not, look, that you may see my Servant, my Messenger whom I send.\"", "Now this is what I would call a CLEAR Prophecy, for those who are actually interested in clear Prophecies. No one in History fits this description, except Prophet Muhammad. No one came to the Arabs, claiming that he's coming on behalf of the God of Abraham, doing exactly these things, except Prophet Muhammad: taking them out of darkness into light, making them praise God in the mountains. Go to Mecca: what do people do in Mecca in Pilgrimage? They praise God! When people go, they say: لبَّيكَ اللهمَّ لبَّيكَ. This is what people do in the mountains. Mecca and Medina are just places where you worship and praise God. These mountains that are talked about there, they're praising God, they recite the Quran there. No one fits this like a glove; it's clear cut, you cannot escape this idea.", "No one can come in history and do anything, because there's no more idol worshipers in the deserts of Arabia. It's been extinct, because God has taken the Glory, as He says in that verse, that this has held for too long, that they've been worshipping idols: \"Now I'm going to take this away; there's not going to be any more worship of idols.\" And it was taken away, so that Prophecy cannot even be fulfilled in the future. It has to be what happened with Prophet Muhammadﷺ.", "And what's interesting is one of the Companions of the Prophetﷺ mentioned some parts of this verse as well, like عبدي (A'bdi: my servant). He mentioned the beginning of the verse, referring that this was in the Torah that he was reading, or not reading, because it wasn't there translated fully, but what he heard from the Rabbis etc. He said that there is a Prophecy that fits Prophet Muhammad. And that Companion mentioned that Prophecy, which is very close to this. Definitely, he was referring to this, because it has some of its wording in the حديث (Hadith: in the Narration) of that Companion.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Shocks Christian Using Old Testament Prophecy! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wm91qI8yjQQ", ((2269, "37:49–38:27"), (2327, "38:47–39:58"), (2429, "40:29–40:53"), (2474, "41:14–42:54"), (2584, "43:04–43:28"), (2614, "43:34–44:18"), (2663, "44:23–45:02"), (2767, "46:07–47:13"), (2833, "47:13–47:42"), (2866, "47:46–48:08"),), id: 1430)
