#passage(("Now, when it comes to Prophet Muhammad, there's an explicit clear cut as sun prophecy in Isaiah, but they still wouldn't accept it.", "That's not an accurate translation. Why? For instance, it says that he will bring forth justice to the Gentiles (Isaiah42:1): it mentions \"Goyim\". I'm sure you heard the name Goyim before: Goyim referring to the Gentiles, which is kind of an insult, by the way, if you are not a Jew.", "He will not cry out or raise his voice: we already know that Jesus cried out, on the cross, allegedly, according to Christians. So this cannot be about him for sure. Then it says, \"a bruised reed not he will break\", and he's not going to be suffering injuries. He will not fail, meaning in his mission he will not fail, he will accomplish his mission.", "And then there's a message here to the Christians, or to the people who don't believe in him, let's just don't say Christians. It says, \"Hear you deaf, you don't hear. Or you're deaf, or you're blind, you don't see.\"", "If you want to apply this to Jesus, you've got to be honest. First, he says he's going to go to the Gentiles. Does that fit Jesus? Or is it exactly the opposite of what Jesus says? He said: \"I was sent to the lost sheep of the house of Israel\" (Mat15:24). Even when he sent his 12 disciples in Matthew, he said: \"Go to the lost sheep of the house of Israel\" (Mat10:5-6). Now, Jesus's mission, who is he sent to? Because here he's talking about someone sent specifically to the Gentiles. Jesus is specifically saying, \"I was not sent\". He's not talking about side missions. He's talking about the MAIN mission.", "Second thing is, it says he's going to bring a NEW Torah. Jesus said in Matthew (Matthew5:17-18): \"I've not come to destroy the law of the Prophets, I've come to fulfil.\" And then he says, \"until heaven and earth pass, no title or dot from the law will be removed.\" He's following the same law. He did not bring a new Torah, for sure.", "When it comes to coming to idol worshippers, did Jesus go out and talk to idol worshippers, and fight against them in war like a mighty man, stirring up his zeal? Did he go to Kedar, the Arabs in Saudi Arabia, Medina? It is impossible for you to fit this as a description of Jesus. You can't, because he never went to that region and he never fought idol worshippers in war and defeated them.", "So if what I told you is true, then what would stop you from accepting Prophet Mohammed as a Messenger of God? You would need a clear guidance from God, and it cannot be the Bible. So that also supports the idea that Prophet Muhammad is a Messenger who came, who told you that the Bible has been changed (the Quran mentions that, anNisa4:46), and told you that God is 1 and not 3 (anNisa4:171), and that people have changed these things (alBaqara2:75-79). So that will just fit that narrative even more.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Gets Questioned On The Treatment Of Women In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jtI_KJQc9SM", ((1714, "28:34–28:38"), (1767, "29:27–29:42"), (1823, "30:23–30:44"), (2052, "34:12–34:24"), (2131, "35:31–36:08"), (2173, "36:13–36:26"), (2192, "36:32–36:55"), (2252, "37:32–38:19"),), id: 1433)
