#passage(("The book in Jay's hand is by Alfred Guillaume, who was a Christian, so when the father is saying nobody dares to publicly question it, he's being absolutely silly, and he's trying to play into this whole conspiracy idea. The reason why Guillaume refers to the book as the life of Muhammad by Muhammad [ibn Ishaq], it's because it's a reconstruction of the original.", "He taught this book to multiple students that wrote it from him. He continued to revise his book, which is why his students have different Renditions of it. His student taught the book to IBN Hisham. This is the most common version of the book today. Other versions can be found elsewhere. The rendition by [Yunus] was printed in the 1970s. Unfortunately both of these experts are oblivious to it.", "I'd also like to add that [Ibn Ishaq] isn't the earliest [Sirah] available to us. I actually have a copy of Suleiman, a student of [Anas] bin Malik, one of these Servants of the Prophet, peace be upon him. The reason why Jay and El Fadi are trying to push back the sources as far as possible is because they want you to believe that everything that we know about Muhammad, peace be upon Him, is unreliable, and so that they can push their Theory.",), "Farid Responds, “\"Prophet Muhammad Didn't Exist!\" [Response Video]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IGyQNmPoiKE", ((130, "2:10–2:32"), (161, "2:41–3:39"), (219, "3:39–4:03"),), id: 1452)
