#passage(("Here is a copy. This one is actually a full copy of the book, written in beautiful font. It starts off with a table of contents. You can actually find the specific copy in the [Süleymaniye] library in Istanbul. This specific copy was written way before [Wüstenfeld] was ever born. And you can find plenty of copies all across the world: you can find them in libraries in Saudi, in the National Library of France, and even the Chester [Beatty] Library in Ireland. So we can't really blame the Germans for everything.", "What Jay needs to be aware of is: the editor for the manuscript is not a scribe; a scribe is not the author. Those are three different occupations or positions. The author is the person who writes the original work. A [copyist] is someone who copies it, or copies a copy of the original work, and the manuscript editor is the person that brings it out to the world for distribution by taking it to a publishing house after editing it. So no, [Wüstenfeld] is not the author.",), "Farid Responds, “Jay Smith: The Germans Created the History of Muhammad!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WeQTguDfY6s", ((463, "7:43–8:23"), (518, "8:38–9:13"),), id: 1453)
