#passage(("First, it's not that I want Prophet Muhammad to be the last Messenger, because I'm not the one who sends Messengers. The One Who sends Prophets and Messengers is God. The One Who determines who's the first Messenger and the last Messenger is God. We are Creation of God, and we obey God. So if God says to us, the X person is the last Messenger, then he is. Well, there has to be a first Messenger and last Messenger anyways, if there's a day of judgement that is going to come. So it just happened to be Prophet Muhammad as the last and final Messenger, and the first Prophet, you can say, was Adam. That was a decision of God.", "In the Bahai tradition, they would say that Prophet Muhammad is a Prophet. But if the Bahai faith claims that Prophet Muhammad is a Messenger of God, or that tradition was right, but then there is another Messenger, [Baha'u'llah], and his progeny and all of that – if they claim that, then how can Prophet Muhammad be a Messenger of God, and he told you he's the last and final Messenger, and then you come and say later on, \"No, he isn't the last and final Messenger\"? If he was a Messenger of God, then he was saying The Truth.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Baha'i Lady Questions Muslim On The Last Prophet! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5_h1_yrAXLg", ((41, "0:41–1:13"), (82, "1:22–1:58"),), id: 1463)
