#passage(("Regarding the Prophetﷺ being the last and final Messenger: Allah sends Prophets and Messengers throughout times. He sent Adam, He sent Abraham, Noah; He sent all of these Prophets and Messengers, and He sent Scriptures with them. Now, the difference between the Message of the Prophetﷺ, Prophet Muhammad, and these Messengers, is that he was sent to everyone, while these previous Messengers were sent to specific localities and people.", "If you look at even what the Bible says in (Matthew15:24), you see Jesus has been only sent to \"the lost sheep of the House of Israel.\" Moses is the same thing: he was sent to the Israelites, taking them out of Egypt to the promised land. And Joshua took them into the promised land, because Moses died before entering. These Prophets and Messengers were sent to certain people, certain localities, and Abraham to ancient Mesopotamia at the time. The Prophetﷺ was sent to EVERYONE.", "Now, because the Prophetﷺ was sent to everyone, his Message was universal, and therefore Allah preserved it. Unlike the previous Messages: Allahﷻ, for example, gave the preservation of the Torah and the Gospels to the priests and the rabbis. Then they failed at this; they changed the Scriptures to gain worldly gains, to get money; they corrupted the Scriptures. But when it comes to the Quran, He preserved it, because it will remain until the Day of Judgment. It will remain there as a Message, as a guidance for the people, until the Day of Judgment.", "Prophet Muhammadﷺ is the last Messenger because his Message is universal and he is the closest, Last Messenger to the Day of Judgment. That is the reason he is the last Messenger. And the Message is preserved; therefore there is no need to send someone else, because the guidance is there. There was a need to send other Messengers because the Message got corrupted later on, or there were only to certain localities, so God sent another Messenger to a different locality. That was the need for more Messengers in the past, and this need is no longer there.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Curious Lady Grills Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2EcJiOmZI44", ((68, "1:08–1:24"), (115, "1:55–2:25"), (147, "2:27–2:50"), (173, "2:53–3:15"),), id: 1464)
