#passage(("There are many things that Prophet Muhammad mentioned. First thing, he said that he's the last and final Messenger, he's the seal of the Messengers. Each Messenger has other Messengers coming, but he's the last seal of the Messengers. And then there are other teachings that Prophet Muhammad told us. He mentioned five things that are unique to him. For example, the earth is all made a place of prayer, so Muslims can pray anywhere, as long as the floor is clean, but Christians pray specifically in the church or the synagogue.", "After him there's the age of communication, easy for the Message to spread to everyone. So, he's the last and final Messenger that is chosen by Allah. All of these are some of the things that Prophet Muhammad told us are specifically unique to him, that was not made for other Messengers of God. But the Quran teaches us we have to believe in all of them. We can't pick and choose. And the Prophet told us explicitly not to compare in a demeaning way between the Messengers. He said: do not say, I'm better than Jonah (Yunus ibn Matta). Why is he saying that? Because people would be fighting and comparing: \"Oh, he's better than him!\" And then problems will happen. That's why the Prophet taught us not to do this, not to be in a comparative way, in a bad way comparing between the Messengers. So, we say he's a Messenger; his job is to give me the Message; I should focus on God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Christians Investigate Islam Part 2! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lC7m3Z_Ms-U", ((1146, "19:06–19:29"), (1194, "19:54–20:42"),), id: 1466)
