#passage(("Here's the thing: if someone says \"we're waiting for Salah\", is there a difference of opinion among the people that Salah is dead and he's never coming back to life? There is no difference of opinion.", "At least you need to be aware – I'm sure you are aware – Christians had this opinion. What's the wisdom behind saying something that supports their belief, that endorses their false ideology? Unfortunately, you have all the commentators literally claiming that this is actually Isa. You even have [Mirza] Ahmed thinking that Isa is gonna be coming back. What he should have done is: the prophet, peace be upon him, keep things simple and say \"a man like Isa\". Instead he gives us three reports, and all it has led to is commentators claiming that [Isa] is going to come back.", "You can have prophecies that are metaphorical in nature; that's fine. But the problem here is we're referring to a prophecy that's used for the authority of someone. So that's a very clear problem, because I could say that this prophecy refers to me.", "Your best answer to this was: it's very clear in the Quran. Well, the only group of people that said that Isa is actually someone like Isa, and not actually Isa, is a group that you have no idea who they are. You can't name them. You can't name a single scholar that held this position. The prophet, again and again, kept on using the words and never made him seem like someone else. All Scholars took it literally, including Ahmed, and the reason for that is because Muhammad said [Isa], and he didn't say \"like\".",), "Farid Responds, “Destroying Qadianis with ONE Question”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=leu0Je7sQA8", ((273, "4:33–4:45"), (294, "4:54–9:16"), (576, "9:36–9:58"), (667, "11:07–15:07"),), id: 1489)
