#passage(("He'd make a prophecy that someone would die, and on the day in which they're supposed to die he'd be like, \"God has forgiven this person\", or \"has delayed the time because this person showed fear\". Or he would claim that his newborn boy is going to be the promised reformer, and then soon after the boy passes away he's like, \"The Revelation actually meant I was going to be given two sons.\" If you want to believe in these cop outs, then be my guest; nobody can force you to believe otherwise. But please don't make such accusations against the actual prophets of God, for they are free from such absurdities.",), "Farid Responds, “If Mirza Ghulam Ahmad made a World Cup prophecy”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PKbizElwAok", ((474, "7:54–8:35"),), id: 1495)
